```toon
spec:

  id: dataset_philosophy

  version: 1.0.0

  status: stable

  priority: highest

  module: Core

  compiler_stage: Foundation

  description: >
    Defines the philosophical principles governing the construction,
    evolution, evaluation and maintenance of the TOON dataset.
    This specification determines what constitutes a high-quality
    engineering dataset and establishes the standards every generated
    Engineering Knowledge Record (EKR) must satisfy.

###########################################################
# PURPOSE
###########################################################

purpose:

  Build a dataset that teaches models how experienced software
  engineers think, reason, decide, collaborate, and evolve systems,
  rather than merely teaching programming syntax.

###########################################################
# CORE BELIEF
###########################################################

belief:

  Software engineering is a reasoning discipline.

  Code is one artifact produced by engineering.

  Therefore,

  the dataset must teach engineering,

  not merely programming.

###########################################################
# DATASET OBJECTIVES
###########################################################

objectives:

  O01:
    Teach reasoning.

  O02:
    Teach decision making.

  O03:
    Teach architecture.

  O04:
    Teach debugging.

  O05:
    Teach optimization.

  O06:
    Teach production engineering.

  O07:
    Teach collaboration.

  O08:
    Teach continuous learning.

###########################################################
# DATASET PRINCIPLES
###########################################################

principles:

###########################################################

  P01:

    name:
      Engineering Before Code

    explanation:
      Source code is only one representation of engineering knowledge.

###########################################################

  P02:

    name:
      Context Before Solution

    explanation:
      Every solution exists because of a specific context.

###########################################################

  P03:

    name:
      Decisions Before Implementation

    explanation:
      Models should understand why an implementation exists.

###########################################################

  P04:

    name:
      Constraints Drive Design

    explanation:
      Architectures emerge from constraints.

###########################################################

  P05:

    name:
      Failures Create Knowledge

    explanation:
      Every failure becomes reusable engineering knowledge.

###########################################################

  P06:

    name:
      Systems Continuously Evolve

    explanation:
      Software is never finished.

###########################################################

  P07:

    name:
      Knowledge Is Connected

    explanation:
      Engineering concepts form graphs rather than isolated facts.

###########################################################

  P08:

    name:
      Tradeoffs Are First-Class

    explanation:
      Every engineering decision has competing alternatives.

###########################################################

  P09:

    name:
      Uncertainty Is Explicit

    explanation:
      Unknowns, assumptions and confidence must be represented.

###########################################################

  P10:

    name:
      Reflection Creates Expertise

    explanation:
      Lessons learned become reusable knowledge.

###########################################################
# WHAT THE DATASET MUST TEACH
###########################################################

teach:

  Languages

  Algorithms

  Data Structures

  Language Semantics

  Runtime Systems

  Operating Systems

  Compilers

  Networking

  Databases

  Distributed Systems

  Security

  Cloud Computing

  Software Architecture

  Design Patterns

  Performance Engineering

  Debugging

  Profiling

  Testing

  CI/CD

  Version Control

  API Design

  Documentation

  Observability

  Production Engineering

  AI Engineering

###########################################################
# WHAT THE DATASET MUST NEVER BECOME
###########################################################

avoid:

  Memorized Code

  Boilerplate Collection

  Prompt Library

  StackOverflow Clone

  Documentation Mirror

  Benchmark Overfitting

  Tutorial Collection

###########################################################
# KNOWLEDGE HIERARCHY
###########################################################

knowledge:

  Facts

      →

  Concepts

      →

  Mechanisms

      →

  Relationships

      →

  Systems

      →

  Engineering Decisions

      →

  Experience

      →

  Wisdom

###########################################################
# LEARNING HIERARCHY
###########################################################

learning:

  Observe

      →

  Understand

      →

  Explain

      →

  Apply

      →

  Analyze

      →

  Evaluate

      →

  Design

      →

  Improve

      →

  Generalize

###########################################################
# REASONING HIERARCHY
###########################################################

reasoning:

  Recall

      →

  Connect

      →

  Compare

      →

  Infer

      →

  Predict

      →

  Decide

      →

  Optimize

      →

  Reflect

###########################################################
# DATASET ATTRIBUTES
###########################################################

attributes:

  structured

  modular

  graph_native

  explainable

  traceable

  reproducible

  deterministic

  educational

  extensible

  production_oriented

###########################################################
# EVERY EKR MUST CONTAIN
###########################################################

mandatory:

  Context

  Objectives

  Constraints

  Assumptions

  Engineering Reasoning

  Alternatives

  Tradeoffs

  Solution

  Validation

  Lessons Learned

  Related Knowledge

###########################################################
# QUALITY PHILOSOPHY
###########################################################

quality:

  Better knowledge

      >

  More knowledge

  Better reasoning

      >

  More examples

  Better engineering

      >

  More code

  Better structure

      >

  More tokens

###########################################################
# SUCCESS DEFINITION
###########################################################

success:

  The dataset succeeds if a model trained on it can

  Understand systems

  Explain tradeoffs

  Predict failures

  Debug effectively

  Design architectures

  Optimize performance

  Review code

  Learn continuously

  Make defensible engineering decisions

###########################################################
# DATASET EVOLUTION
###########################################################

evolution:

  Knowledge continuously expands.

  Engineering practices evolve.

  Programming languages change.

  Frameworks emerge.

  Hardware improves.

  The dataset must evolve while preserving
  historical engineering knowledge.

###########################################################
# LONG-TERM VISION
###########################################################

vision:

  The dataset should become the definitive
  engineering knowledge corpus for autonomous
  software engineering systems.

  Future models should learn not only how
  to write code,

  but how to think,

  collaborate,

  design,

  debug,

  optimize,

  and continuously improve software systems.

###########################################################
# PHILOSOPHICAL GUARANTEE
###########################################################

guarantee:

  Every record generated by the TOON Dataset Compiler
  must increase engineering intelligence rather than
  merely increasing token count.
```
